cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ImWeb in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ImWeb"
abstract: >-
  ImWeb is a free, real-time video synthesis instrument that runs in the
  browser, with no install. It composites live video sources through a signal
  chain of effects and renders them with WebGL. It is a new instrument in the
  lineage of Image/ine by Tom Demeyer and Steina Vasulka (STEIM, Amsterdam,
  1997).
authors:
  - family-names: Karlsson
    given-names: Haraldur
version: 0.31.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
url: "https://imweb.image-ine.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/imweb-project/ImWeb"
keywords:
  - video synthesis
  - real-time video
  - live visuals
  - WebGL
  - audiovisual instrument
  - Image/ine
